From 1a220cb2db15c4d142f2ee8a97fa111b42d7d806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: drop the stale-race floor/wall step from
 borg_new_kill()

borg_new_kill() took r_ptr from the tracking slot before storing the new
race in it, so the closing "force the grid to floor / granite" step read
the slot's previous race: race 0 for a wiped slot (or an older race after
borg_kills_nxt is reset without wiping the array). With race 0 the step
always marks the grid as floor, so a pass-wall monster first seen inside
rock turns that rock into floor in the Borg's map. The ranged-attack
check "never shoot walls" then lets the Borg fire at the monster, and the
game stops the missile in front of the wall: the turn and the ammunition
are lost.

borg_update_kill_old(n), called a few lines earlier with the correct
race, already performs this step, keeping a seen floor grid as floor and
otherwise marking the grid as granite for a pass-wall monster. Remove
the duplicate step and the two locals that only it used.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#95.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c | 18 ------------------
 1 file changed, 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
index 0c347c5ad..cd99a3de9 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
@@ -711,8 +711,6 @@ static int borg_new_kill(unsigned int r_idx, int y, int x)
     int i, n = -1;
 
     borg_kill           *kill;
-    borg_grid           *ag;
-    struct monster_race *r_ptr;
     struct monster      *m_ptr;
 
     /* Look for a "dead" monster */
@@ -750,8 +748,6 @@ static int borg_new_kill(unsigned int r_idx, int y, int x)
 
     /* Access the monster */
     kill  = &borg_kills[n];
-    r_ptr = &r_info[kill->r_idx];
-    ag    = &borg_grids[y][x];
 
     /* Save the race */
     kill->r_idx = r_idx;
@@ -824,20 +820,6 @@ static int borg_new_kill(unsigned int r_idx, int y, int x)
         && borg_los(kill->pos.y, kill->pos.x, borg.c.y, borg.c.x))
         borg.goal.type = 0;
 
-    /* Force the monster to be sitting on a floor
-     * grid unless that monster can pass through walls
-     */
-    if (!(rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_PASS_WALL))) {
-        ag->feat = FEAT_FLOOR;
-    }
-
-    /* Force the ghostly monster to be in a wall
-     * grid until the grid is proven to be something else
-     */
-    if (rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_PASS_WALL)) {
-        ag->feat = FEAT_GRANITE;
-    }
-
     /* Count up out list of Nasties */
     for (i = 0; i < borg_nasties_num; i++) {
         /* Count them up */
-- 
